  "note": "Election of the Cookstown Urban District Council, ordinary triennial election 21 May 1958; twelve persons validly nominated for twelve seats, no contest (Mid-Ulster Mail, 10 May 1958, p. 2). Official returning-officer statement: 'URBAN DISTRICT — COOKSTOWN ... ORDINARY TRIENNIAL ELECTION, 1958. THE PERSONS WHOSE NAMES, PLACES OF ABODE AND DESCRIPTION ARE SET OUT BELOW HAVE BEEN VALIDLY NOMINATED.' Twelve names for twelve seats; no poll. No party label is printed. Returned unopposed."
